# Testing standards

## Coverage target

**Minimum 90% line coverage** on `lib/`, `services/`, `hooks/`, and `app/api/`.  
UI components: test behaviour, not implementation details.

## Stack

- **Vitest** + **@testing-library/react** for unit/integration tests
- **@vitest/coverage-v8** for coverage reports

```bash
npm i -D vitest @vitest/coverage-v8 @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom
```

`vitest.config.ts`:

```ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    environment: "jsdom",
    setupFiles: ["./tests/setup.ts"],
    include: ["tests/**/*.test.ts", "tests/**/*.test.tsx"],
    coverage: {
      provider: "v8",
      thresholds: { lines: 90, branches: 85, functions: 90, statements: 90 },
      include: ["lib/**", "services/**", "hooks/**", "app/api/**"],
      exclude: ["**/*.d.ts", "**/types/**"],
    },
  },
});
```

## What to test

| Layer | Focus |
|-------|-------|
| `lib/` | Pure functions — edge cases, invalid input, round-trips |
| `services/` | Mock external APIs; verify request shape and error handling |
| `hooks/` | State transitions, loading/error paths |
| `app/api/` | Auth rejection (401/403), validation errors (400), happy path |
| `components/` | User-visible behaviour — render, click, form submit |

## Test file conventions

- **Centralized in `tests/`** — mirror source layout:
  - `lib/bereken-niveau.ts` → `tests/lib/bereken-niveau.test.ts`
  - `hooks/useOntwikkelpaden.ts` → `tests/hooks/useOntwikkelpaden.test.tsx`
  - `app/api/health/route.ts` → `tests/app/api/health/route.test.ts`
- Shared mocks/fixtures live in `tests/helpers/`
- Name: `<module>.test.ts` — no `.spec` mixing within one project
- No tests that only assert "renders without crashing"
- Do not colocate `*.test.ts` next to source files

## CI

```json
"test": "vitest run",
"test:coverage": "vitest run --coverage"
```

Block merge if coverage drops below thresholds.
